    "updated_at": "2026-09-22T05:09:46Z",
    "body": "Hi @arpera, thanks for the review! Done:\n\n- **Description corrected**: since #47312, grammar compilation failures finish as per-request errors instead of tearing down the engine, so I reworded the motivation — this PR now purely adds the validation-layer rejection (clean 400, consistent with the existing `json=\"\"`/`grammar=\"\"` guards) and closes the `regex=\"\"` silent no-op (xgrammar tolerates `compile_regex(\"\")`, so it currently returns 200 while constraining nothing). Title updated accordingly.\n- **Rebased** on the latest main.\n- **pre-commit** (`ruff check`, `ruff format`, `mypy`, typos) passes on both changed files.\n\nUnit tests: all 22 cases in `tests/v1/structured_output/test_validation.py` pass, including the two new degenerate-input cases.",
